```text
================================
PHASE 3: REFACTORING COMPLETE
================================
## New Project Structure
app.py (create_app, entry point) · seed.py · .env.example
config/       settings.py, constants.py
models/       database.py, base.py, task.py, user.py, category.py
routes/       task, user, category, report, health  (URL → controller)
controllers/  task, user, category, report, health
middlewares/  error_handler.py, auth.py
services/     notification_service.py
utils/        dates.py, validators.py

## Changes Applied
AP-01/AP-15 → config/settings.py reads environment variables; debug is off by default; no secrets in the code
AP-04 → admin_required on the three DELETEs and on PUT /users when it changes role or active (PB-10)
AP-05 → scrypt hashing; legacy md5/plain passwords still log in and are re-hashed on login; password removed from responses; signed token
AP-07/09 → controllers added; /categories moved to its own routes file and controller; serialization and validation centralized
AP-10 → joinedload and GROUP BY queries replace the per-row queries
AP-11/12 → central error handler returns JSON; priority, date and query-parameter input is validated
AP-13/16/17 → is_overdue used everywhere; constants; logging instead of print; unused helpers and imports removed
DP-01 → utcnow helper and db.session.get replace the deprecated calls

## Validation
  ✓ Application boots without errors
  ✓ All endpoints respond correctly (32/32 baseline calls, same status codes and JSON structure; the only differences are the removed password field)
  ✓ CRITICAL findings fixed: 3/3 (verified by search; the only md5 left is the legacy login check)
  ✓ Login works on a database created by the original version (md5 passwords)
  ✓ Admin token tested: 403 without or with a wrong token, 200 with it, 403 in production with no token set

## Intentional behavior changes
- `password` is no longer in the responses of POST /users, GET /users/<id>, PUT /users/<id> and /login (AP-05).
- The login `token` is now a signed token instead of `fake-jwt-token-<id>`.
- Debug now defaults to off (AP-01).
- DELETE /tasks, /users, /categories and PUT /users with `role` or `active` check `X-Admin-Token` (AP-04). If `ADMIN_TOKEN` isn't set, they still work outside production and log a warning. In production they return 403.
- Invalid types that used to cause 500 errors now return 400: string priority, non-numeric `priority` or `user_id` in /tasks/search, empty body on PUT /categories, non-boolean `active`, empty `name`.

## Remaining findings
- No real authentication or authorization on any route (out of scope).
- Category `color` is not validated, because rejecting values would change what the API accepts today.
- AP-14 correction: for categories, SQLAlchemy already clears `category_id` on a category's tasks when it is deleted, so that part of the finding was a false positive. User deletion now cascades to their tasks in one transaction.
- `NotificationService` is still not wired into any route. I kept it and moved its credentials to configuration.
- `requirements.txt` lists `marshmallow` and `requests`, which nothing uses. I did not touch it.
================================
